    "done_when": "Deliver §2 of docs/plans/lane-and-model-routing.html exactly as that section states. The plan and its locked decisions are the authority. §1 is on main: reckon/schema/flight.yaml declares lanes, and reckon/flight.py expands them.\n\n1. docs/state/reckon/model-catalogue.yaml regroups its eight backend entries under lanes, each with a default model:\n   - claude holds sonnet, opus and haiku.\n   - codex holds sol, astra and luna.\n   - clive holds its local model.\n   Keep the existing backends blocks, so the new resolution can be compared directly with the old one.\n2. Add the alias table §7 reads. It maps claude-opus, claude-haiku, codex-astra, codex-luna, codex-terra, codex-spark and clive-glm each to a lane and a model key. If the catalogue schema has no slot for that table, add it to the LinkML source reckon/schema/flight.yaml. Then regenerate reckon/_flight_schema.py and docs/_shared/flight.schema.json with scripts/regen_flight_schema.py, with PATH=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin:$PATH. Never hand-edit the two generated files.\n3. tests/test_catalogue_declares_lanes.py asserts every alias resolves to a declared lane and model.\n4. reckon flight --project reckon output is identical to base, and the catalogue provenance shows the same leaves as before. Keep both outputs under the run directory.\n5. Negative control: deleting one model entry makes the identity check fail.\n6. Also close one follow-on from §1's review. LANE_MODEL_KEYS in reckon/flight.py hand-copies LaneModelConfig's field list. Derive it from the generated model, or add a test that the two match.\n\nGate: tests/test_catalogue_declares_lanes.py, every tests/test_flight*.py, and every tests/ file that imports reckon.capabilities or reads model-catalogue.yaml. Build that list from your head tree with grep -l. Run with PATH=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin:$PATH /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, so the LinkML round-trip tests run rather than skip. Keep one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta. Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/lane-and-model-routing/catalogue-declares-lanes.html.",
